        "prompt": "Some people believe that artificial intelligence will create more job opportunities than it eliminates, while others argue it will cause widespread unemployment. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.",
        "model_answer": "The rapid proliferation of artificial intelligence (AI) across diverse industries has ignited intense discourse regarding its long-term ramifications for the global workforce. While some commentators argue that AI will automate vast swathes of employment and trigger mass joblessness, others maintain that it will serve as an engine of innovation, generating novel career paths. In my view, although structural displacement will cause short-term disruption, AI will ultimately create a more dynamic and prosperous employment landscape.\n\nOn the one hand, proponents of the unemployment hypothesis point out that machine-learning algorithms and robotic automation are increasingly capable of executing complex analytical and manual tasks. Routine administrative functions, customer service, data entry, and even basic programming are progressively being outsourced to automated systems. For mid-career professionals lacking technical adaptability, this transition can result in prolonged job displacement and widening socio-economic disparity, especially if retraining initiatives fail to keep pace with algorithmic advancements.\n\nOn the other hand, historical technological revolutions—such as the Industrial Revolution and the advent of the internet—demonstrate that while obsolete roles disappear, entirely new industrial sectors inevitably emerge. AI deployment necessitates an immense workforce specialized in algorithmic auditing, cybersecurity, ethical AI governance, prompt engineering, and human-machine collaboration. Furthermore, by automating mundane operations, AI elevates human productivity, enabling businesses to scale rapidly and reinvest capital into research, creative disciplines, and personalized customer experiences, which inherently require human empathy.\n\nIn conclusion, while the transition phase undeniably poses acute challenges for routine-based occupations, I believe AI will fundamentally expand the global economic frontier and generate far more high-value, creative, and technical career opportunities than it renders obsolete.",
